BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Wrecks in the water</h1>
With the damage simulation on, over the open Atlantic: a delta-glider dives
into the sea at 150 m/s, 30 deg nose down, and breaks up; its pieces are
flooded and sink to the nominal seabed (40 m), where they come to rest.
Another falls from 5 km under time acceleration (limited to 10x in the
air) and hits the water at its terminal speed: destroyed.
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 51982.6685767396
  Script Tests/WaterSinkTest
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship OBS
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
